I was getting super annoyed that there is nothing between 1 and 1.25x on the vimeo video player, so I just used a simple command after looking through the DOM now I can adjust the speed while I watch the video with my keyboard Here's how to use it if you're facing the same annoyance as me.

Instructions:

[ol:1][li]Right-click on the video while it’s playing, then click “Inspect”.[li]In the panel that opens, click the “Console” tab.[li]Copy and paste the code below into the console:
document.addEventListener\('keydown', function\(e\) {
const video = document.querySelector\('video'\);
if \(!video\) return;

if \(e.key === '.'\) {
video.playbackRate = Math.min\(video.playbackRate + 0.05, 16\);
console.log\('Speed increased to:', video.playbackRate.toFixed\(2\)\);
}

if \(e.key === ','\) {
video.playbackRate = Math.max\(video.playbackRate - 0.05, 0.1\);
console.log\('Speed decreased to:', video.playbackRate.toFixed\(2\)\);
}
}\);

[ol:1][li]Press . \(period\) to speed up the video.[li]Press , \(comma\) to slow it down.[li]The current speed will be printed in the console.

